ORFik 1.29.17
=============

Optimized annotation files
--------------------------

    o Bug fix: makeTxdbFromGenome(optimize = TRUE) named the ORFik_optimized
      files after the txdb path (<gtf>.db_<time>_cds.qs), while loadRegion()
      and optimizedTranscriptLengths() looked for <gtf>_<time>_cds.qs, so the
      optimized files were never used. The writer now uses <gtf>_<time>, and
      the reader also accepts the legacy <gtf>.db_<time> and old
      <gtf without extension>_<time> prefixes.

Bioconductor devel compatibility
--------------------------------

    o Bug fix for GenomicRanges >= 1.65.2 (Bioconductor 3.24): as.data.frame() of
      a GRanges now returns names(x) as a "names" column instead of row names, so
      a "names" meta column appeared twice. gSort()/sortPerGroup() then kept the
      transcript names instead of the ORF names (tx1 instead of tx1_1), and
      assignFirst/LastExonsStopSite() failed ("Can't assign to the same column
      twice"). Internal grDT() drops range names before conversion; used in
      gSort, assignFirstExonsStartSite, assignLastExonsStopSite,
      unlistToExtremities, findMaxPeaks, removeTxdbExons, import.fstwig and
      export.bedo (which no longer writes a names column on new Bioconductor).
    o Tests: detect_ribo_orfs tests no longer leave libraries in .GlobalEnv; the
      real-signal OFST scratch test is skipped on CRAN/Bioconductor builders.
    o Rd files regenerated for countOverlapsW, detect_ribo_orfs,
      detectRibosomeShifts_new and detectRibosomeShifts_index.

Codon dwell times
-----------------

    o New codon_dwell(): log relative ribosome dwell time per codon at offsets
      around the A site (default -10..+5 codons), per library. Profiled-gene
      quasi-Poisson GLM (gene effects removed exactly by conditioning on gene
      totals, Fisher scoring on beta only, gene-clustered sandwich SEs),
      sum-to-zero betas per offset, in-sample and held-out deviance explained.
      C++ kernel with OpenMP threads. method = "ratio" gives the codon_usage()
      (mean_txNorm) estimate for the P and A site.
    o New codon_dwell_design(): the sequence-only design (built once per
      annotation, reusable across libraries) and codon_dwell_plot() (offset x
      codon heatmap, or bars at one offset with 95% CI).
    o codon_dwell(end_bias = TRUE): optional footprint end bias correction
      (choros-style technical terms). P-sites are split by read length and
      P-site frame; per read length, the nucleotides at and next to the 5' and
      3' read ends (and the flanking cut-site nucleotides) are fitted within
      codon positions, where dwell and gene flux cancel, and reads are
      reweighted before the codon fit. Needs the read lengths ("size" column of
      pshifted ofst files) and the P-site offsets (shifts, default
      shifts_load(df)). end_bias = TRUE models 3 nt per end plus the flanking
      cut-site nt; an integer 1..6 sets the number of nt. Attribute "end_bias"
      holds the end terms. On eIF5A / DOHH KO and WT libraries (PRJNA545625)
      the spread of betas at the footprint-end offsets shrinks (-6: 40 %,
      -5: 46 %, +3: 18 %, +4: 38 %, +5: 48 %), interior offsets (-4..+2) stay
      within +-11 %, and the Pro effects at E and P stay (eIF5A KO - WT at P:
      0.171 -> 0.180).
    o codon_dwell(): P-sites are mapped to codons through a genome position
      index stored in the design (findInterval on sorted CDS exons, overlapping
      CDSs in layers, one C++ pass) instead of findOverlaps +
      pmapToTranscriptF. The counts are identical and mapping is 4-5x faster
      (21.5M CDS P-sites on a loaded host: 12-13 s -> 2-4 s).
      The fit starts from marginal ratio estimates and refreshes the Hessian
      until the step is below 0.02 (fewer information-matrix passes, same
      optimum, |delta beta| < 1e-9). End to end, a 21.5M CDS P-site library at
      4 threads takes 7.6-8.9 s instead of 26 s (27-32 s on the same loaded
      host). Designs saved by older versions get the index built on the fly.

Other changes merged in 1.29.17
-------------------------------

    o findFromPath(): a unique file-name match wins over directory-name hits
      (template experiments with non-unique names).
    o coveragePerTiling(): opt-in keep.names = "factor" keeps names in the data.table.
    o STAR alignment: optional ORFIK_STAR_EXTRA_ARGS environment variable for the genome step.
    o Fast derived formats: ofst_derive() writes covRleList, covRle, bigWig and count
      tables in one pass (Rle kernel, parallel bigWig writer, OFST block index).
    o OFST store: incremental merges (mergeLibs(base, subtract), ofst_store_*()),
      delta updates and streaming export (uses fst::concat_fst when available).

ORFik 1.29.16
=============

Ribo-seq ORF detection
----------------------

    o detect_ribo_orfs(): about 3x faster per library on covRle input (HEK293 MANE
      candidates, 100 merged libraries: 30 s -> 9.5 s; tables identical). ORF,
      upstream and downstream statistics are computed in one C++ pass over the
      covRle runs (orfStatsCovRleCPP) instead of a per-nucleotide data.table, gene
      names are joined with chmatch, and with several libraries the annotation-only
      columns (start codons, transcript positions) are computed once.
    o detect_ribo_orfs(upstream_filter = "non_annotated"): new option that skips
      the upstream-window rule for annotated CDSs (default "all" = old behaviour).
    o Bug fix: rows of transcripts without a gene symbol could be misaligned in
      the prediction table (merge(all.x, sort = FALSE) moved them to the end).

Transcript mapping and accessors
-------------------------------

    o Bug fix: empty transcript ranges (end = start - 1) map again to empty genomic
      ranges, as before the C++ rewrite. windowPerGroup() upstream of an ORF that
      starts at transcript position 1 or 2 failed with "Transcript query
      coordinates are out of bounds", which made detect_ribo_orfs() fail on
      full candidate sets.
    o Mapping validation, mixed-strand preparation, interval reduction and
      output factories now run in C++ bindings. A standalone C++11 header
      separates coordinate logic from R/Rcpp objects; input storage is borrowed.
      Full-call and storage-representation benchmarks, original baselines and
      reproduction notes live in benchmark/transcript_mapping/.

    o Paired transcript mapping borrows integer inputs and writes final output
      vectors directly. Long ordered exon searches use binary lookup; short
      and irregular groups retain bounded linear searches.
    o Mapping checks transcript boundaries, empty inputs, coordinate overflow,
      paired chromosomes and scalar references. Unmappable genomic queries
      retain the existing sentinel; invalid transcript queries report errors.
    o The to-transcript wrapper reads unlisted strand and partition offsets
      directly. Group strand/sequence accessors index Rle values before
      expansion only for large, exon-rich lists, retaining the small-list path.

Coverage performance
--------------------

    o coverageByTranscriptFST batches chromosome-aware page/exon joins and
      shares bounded reads of nearby page slices within a call. Input exon
      order, requested column order, strand reversal and independent result
      tables are preserved. Indexes/pages are reread on every call.
    o coverage_to_dt expands positive coverage runs directly, avoiding a
      one-base IRanges object per output row. Counts, gene factors, positions,
      frame columns and empty-coverage warnings are preserved.

ORFik 1.0.0
-----------------------

    o first release of ORFik - find Open Reading Frames, automatic RiboSeq
    footprint shifts, reassignment of Transcription Start Sites with the use of
    CageSeq, plethora of gene identity functions from scientific publications

Bioconductor build fixes
-----------------------

    o Genome download failures now report the underlying service error instead
      of failing while coercing an error object to a logical value.
    o The importing-data and transcript tutorials use bundled synthetic
      references for runnable examples; network download examples remain
      available as explicit, optional steps. All vignettes include session info.
    o Reference-space CIGAR widths now use cigarillo on current Bioconductor,
      with a compatibility fallback for older releases, as query-space widths do.
    o Clarified local-reference arguments, cache reuse and pseudo-leader
      interpretation, and corrected the fastp UMI example.


CHANGES IN VERSION 1.1.12
-----------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o Remade many function to handle no names correctly, like tile1 will now
    work even for GRangesList without names. Documentation is more logical, and
    removed coverageByWindow, since GenomicFeatures::coverageByTranscripts now
    works correctly.

CHANGES IN VERSION 1.1.12
-------------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o The orf finding function now find the longest orf per stop codon if
      you set longestORF = TRUE in findORFS, findMapORFs and findORFsFasta

CHANGES IN VERSION 1.3.7
-------------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o mapToGRanges is now much faster and uses much less memory. A c++
      reimplementation of pmapFromTranscripts from GenomicFeatures.

CHANGES IN VERSION 1.7.0
-------------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o The ORFik experiment syntax is ready, to simplifiy ORFik usage
    with big data.


CHANGES IN VERSION 1.7.17
-------------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o Added pmapToTranscriptsF, a much faster pmapToTranscripts.
    o All of ORFik now supports weights for representing duplicated reads.
    This will speed up all function related to NGS data a lot.

CHANGES IN VERSION 1.13.7
-------------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o Massive improvement in speed of coveragePerTiling
    o Improved p-shifting analysis (also added verbose output)
    o Added possible optimization for annotation
    o Rewritten vignettes

CHANGES IN VERSION 1.23.8
-------------------------

SIGNIFICANT USER-VISIBLE CHANGES

    o Implemented a Ribo-seq ORF detector now included
    o Added new export functions for bigwig, covRLE

STAR / fastp updates
-------------------

    o Fixed allow.introns forwarding in STAR.align.single and STAR.align.folder.
      The default TRUE now enables novel junction discovery (--alignIntronMax 0).
      Earlier affected runs silently used 1 even with TRUE. Set FALSE explicitly
      to retain that indexed-junction-only behavior; indexed splicing remains
      possible in either mode. This correction can change alignment results.
    o Added base.correction = FALSE to both entry points. TRUE enables fastp
      correction of overlapping paired reads during trimming (issue #172).
    o Pipeline logs now show each step's actual inputs, outputs and command,
      instead of repeatedly presenting the original reads as input (issue #174).
    o Fixed paired-folder multimapping option forwarding, tRNA input compression,
      and noShared memory mode across multiple libraries. Commands preserve paths
      containing spaces or shell metacharacters and stop on tool failure.
    o Empty folders, duplicate output basenames, and invalid step order now fail
      explicitly. Pairing still uses adjacent files in sorted filename order.
